    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch12-01: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.07";
    dc:description "Calling a rule-following process a computation does not add a variable, a dataset, or a forbidden outcome. Whether nature in fact follows definite rules is a different and stronger statement than the one made here. As stated, the sentence is a framework for comparison, not a claim those comparisons can test.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The claim says every rule-governed process may be regarded as a computation. Any process already given by definite rules satisfies that redescription, and no measurement distinguishes it from the same process described as law-governed evolution.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
